$split_song — split audio at low vocal activity

SUMMARY
  Takes sounds[] (full mix), separates the vocal stem, measures voice activity on
  that stem, and splits the original audio into WAV segments. Each segment is at
  most period= seconds long and at least period/2 seconds (internal cuts are placed
  at the quietest vocal point in each allowed window).

SYNTAX
  $split_song(period=30)
  $split_song(period=45, model=bs_roformer_viperx_1297)

INPUT
  sounds[] — one or more audio files (wav, mp3, …).

OUTPUT
  sounds[] — replaced with segment WAV links (original mix slices, not vocal-only).

ARGUMENTS
  period=     — max segment length in seconds (required semantics; default 30).
                Min segment length = period / 2.
  model=      — vocal separation model (default bs_roformer_viperx_1297 / 2stem).
  model_path= — optional local RoFormer checkpoint (same as $music_separation).
  frame=      — vocal activity frame size in seconds (default 0.05).

DEPENDENCIES
  Same as $music_separation: .venvs/media, audio-separator, ffmpeg for non-WAV.

ENVIRONMENT
  AH_EMULATE_SPLIT_SONG=1 — stub segment files without loading models.

EXAMPLE
  @parts: $file('test_data/music/20260524_185140_st_music_0.wav') -> $split_song(period=30)

  See examples/example_split_song.ah

PROMPT-CONSUMING
  No.
